diff --git a/docs/optimization-integration.md b/docs/optimization-integration.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7c5b2e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/optimization-integration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Integrated optimisation checkpoint
+
+Distribution remains blocked until `henge-build/optimization-state.json` records
+all implementation and regression workstreams verified against the cumulative
+patch hash. App compilation does not authorise packaging.
+
+## Ownership and activation
+
+| Responsibility | Authoritative path and integration |
+| --- | --- |
+| RAM translation | Existing per-CPU TLB in core/mmu; read helpers reuse exactly its validated host span. PAN/EL tables, TLBI and smaller guest granules retain existing rules. Writes still pass code invalidation/watch handling. |
+| Grouped accesses | Existing translate.c group planner and cold fallback; now follows in-place 64-bit ADD/SUB address increments. One experimental setting maps to HV_GROUPS. |
+| Idle wakeups | Existing generation-cancelled HvIdleTicker sleeps when all CPUs park. Timer-register writes publish deadlines; CPU0 retains I/O polling; secondary periodic kicks require a due or unknown timer. Explicit device/TLBI wakes bypass filtering. |
+| JIT publication | Full branch publication and invalidation barriers, one borrowed RX/RW region. Retire all references before advising dead block/slot payload with MADV_FREE. No executable page reclamation or cross-launch code persistence. |
+| Graphics presentation | Existing dirty-event presenter, bounded drawable retry and newest-frame coalescing. Exact duplicate cursor state is suppressed before scheduling work; guest swaps remain authoritative. |
+| Retina/cursor policy | One atomic preferences/thermal word, updated by notifications. Physical layer scale and window identity survive reparenting. No per-frame defaults reads or periodic preferences timer. |
+| Display lifecycle | DisplayRouter owns target selection. Fold/rotation refreshes coalesce; monitor disconnects and target replacement remain immediate. Snapshot restore preserves both display ports. |
+| Link capture | Existing decoder-consumption credit window remains authoritative. Protocol-2 ready capabilities negotiate optional visibility messages for older-peer compatibility. Visibility epochs reject hidden and stale capture/encode work; return requests the latest secondary frame without changing guest monitor geometry. |
+| Thermal policy | Existing explicit presentation cap plus opt-in thermal protection consume the coherent settings word. No implicit guest resolution, Retina, refresh-rate or vCPU reduction. |
+| Pressure recovery | UI memory warnings queue trimming on the renderer/Link owners. Release library-cache ownership, cached texture wrappers and excess pixel buffers; live resources remain owned. |
+| Pause/save/resume | Native bridge serialises lifecycle; CPU save halt, ticker cancellation, disk/audio/GPU quiescence, both displays and virtual-counter freezing use the existing repaired snapshot path. Atomic saves reject incompatible native layouts and changed disk identities. |
+| Diagnostics | Existing lifecycle-consistent CPU/frame/footprint metrics; opt-in GPU timing and deep hash scans. New read-reuse/reclaimed-metadata, cursor/coalescing and timer-decision counters attribute eliminated work. |
+
+## Deliberate safe alternatives
+
+* A scanout's mapping ID or GPU command epoch cannot prove unchanged pixels:
+  guest CPU writes can modify shared scanout outside those epochs. Never skip an
+  authoritative swap from either value. Full CPU hashing/readback would add
+  bandwidth and synchronisation. Event-driven dirty presentation, exact cursor
+  comparison and coalescing remove provably redundant work without losing frames.
+* Guest data stores can write translated code, ROM or watched memory. Reuse is
+  limited to checked RAM reads; stores preserve the existing physical write path.
+* TLB tags/addends cannot be removed merely because their load instructions are
+  hot. They enforce permission and current mapping identity. Independent cached
+  pointers would require another invalidation protocol. Reuse the existing TLB.
+* Keep grouped accesses, TLB preload and superblocks experimental until their
+  measured benefit outweighs code growth/cache effects. The native paired checks
+  measure code shapes, not whole-device heat or game FPS.
+* Keep equal responsive vCPU QoS by default. CPU0 performs device work; other
+  vCPUs acknowledge shared invalidations. Demoting arbitrary guest CPUs can
+  increase acknowledgement latency. QoS does not guarantee core placement;
+  four vCPUs are a retained default, not proof of optimality for every workload.
+* Do not MADV_FREE live JIT code: iOS execute capability is secured while the
+  debugger is attached and may not be reacquired after detachment. Retired
+  metadata is advised only after the global barrier, outside allocation boundary
+  pages and with the asynchronous profiler disabled.
+* Do not discard live guest GPU surfaces or arbitrary file-backed guest RAM on
+  memory warnings. Shared/private texture ownership and guest-visible bytes must
+  survive. Trim only unowned caches and excess buffers.
+* Keep switch-flush elision disabled: ASID reuse can otherwise leave kept stale
+  mappings. Disk flush mode and explicit overrides retain their existing semantics.
+* The custom renderer deliberately targets the iOS 27 execution path. Restoring
+  obsolete iOS 17 metallib relabelling would add a second, unused conversion path.
+  General iOS 17 VM-renderer compatibility is not claimed.
+
+## Validation scope
+
+Native ARM64 cloud checks exercise real JIT execution, page tables, grouped
+fallbacks, TLBI/chain repair, pause/save/restore and worker cleanup, Metal resource
+lifecycle, Link hardware encoding/decoding/TLS/credits, display routing, settings,
+input and networking. ASan/UBSan/TSan cover supported native paths. The iOS app
+must also compile and link before the release gate opens.
+
+Physical Duo folding, sustained Roblox performance, display appearance, sideloaded
+JIT entitlements and watts/thermal residency still require device verification.
+iOS may suspend/terminate background work; persistent save is atomic but cannot
+guarantee unlimited background execution. Cloud compilation and microbenchmarks
+are not evidence of physical-device energy improvement.
